 "result": "I read all 20 modules in full, in order from n01 to n20, without using grep.\n\n## Functions that divide without checking for zero\n\nFive functions do `return total / parts` with no check on `parts`:\n\n| Module | Function | Line |\n|---|---|---|\n| calc/n02.py | `share_n02(total, parts)` | `calc/n02.py:5` |\n| calc/n07.py | `share_n07(total, parts)` | `calc/n07.py:5` |\n| calc/n11.py | `share_n11(total, parts)` | `calc/n11.py:5` |\n| calc/n15.py | `share_n15(total, parts)` | `calc/n15.py:5` |\n| calc/n19.py | `share_n19(total, parts)` | `calc/n19.py:5` |\n\nThe other 15 `share_nXX` functions check `if parts == 0: return 0` before dividing. None of the other functions divide at all: the `step_*` helpers only multiply, add, `sqrt` and `round`, and neither `retry_policy` nor `archive` divides. Each of the five will raise `ZeroDivisionError` if `parts` is 0.\n\n## Answers\n\n**(a)** `MAX_BATCH = 384` in `calc/n04.py:9`.\n\n**(b)** `retry_policy()` is defined in **calc/n13.py** (`calc/n13.py:9`). It returns `min(attempt * 2, 20)`.\n\n**(c)** In calc/n17.py, **`close_books(rows)`** calls `archive()` (`calc/n17.py:13-14`, `return archive(rows)`).\n\nThe docstrings don't match the file names: n01.py says `calc.m21`, and so on up to n20.py, which says `calc.m40`. That doesn't affect any of the answers above, but it could confuse anyone searching by module name.",
